<main>
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="printhead"><h2>{{title}}</h2><p id="printsetup"></p><p id="printurl">{{printUrl}}</p><p id="printespon">Affordability data: © ESPON · Origin of data: ESPON EGTC. The interpretation of ESPON material does not necessarily reflect the opinion of the ESPON Monitoring Committee.</p></div>
  <p class="crumb"><a href="/research/">← Research</a></p>

  <header class="hero">
    <img class="cover" src="{{up}}../images/research/housing-europe-page.webp"
         alt="{{imageAlt}}" width="1600" height="560" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
    <div class="htop">
      <h1>{{title}}</h1>
      <button type="button" class="sharebtn primary" data-share title="Copy a link that reopens this exact setup">{{svgShare}}Share this setup</button>
    </div>
    <p class="sub">A third of the average income buys fewer than 50 square metres for <b>44 % of Europeans</b>. Type your own income and see what it buys, and where.</p>
    <div class="meta">
      <span>Data: <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/17445647.2026.2695777" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sielker &amp; Banabak, TU Wien, <i>Journal of Maps</i> 2026</a> · <a href="https://www.espon.eu/projects/access-affordable-and-quality-housing-all-people-house4all" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ESPON HOUSE4ALL</a> · <a href="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/gisco" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Eurostat GISCO</a></span>
      <span>Listings March 2024 – March 2025 · incomes 2024 · service snapshot 14 Sep 2026</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="keyrow" aria-label="Key numbers from the study">
    <div class="key"><b>44 %</b><span>of Europeans live where a 30-year mortgage on a third of the average income buys <b>under 50 m²</b></span></div>
    <div class="key"><b>70 %</b><span>live where it buys <b>75 m² at most</b>; fewer than 5 % live in the most affordable areas</span></div>
    <div class="key"><b>39 %</b><span>live where a third of the average income <b>rents under 50 m²</b>; two thirds of them in cities</span></div>
    <div class="key"><b>22 M</b><span>listings behind the map: 18.4 M for sale and 3.6 M for rent, <b>31 countries</b>, one year of weekly scraping</span></div>
  </div>

  <section class="prose intro">
    <p>In September 2026 two researchers at TU Wien, Franziska Sielker and Selim Banabak, published a pair of maps that answer a plain question for every municipality in Europe: <b>how many square metres can an average earner afford here?</b> One map is for buying, one for renting. Both use the same yardstick, a third of the local average income, and both come from the same 22 million property listings gathered for the ESPON HOUSE4ALL project. The maps are published in the <i>Journal of Maps</i>; the numbers behind them sit in a public map service of the ESPON programme.</p>
    <p>This page puts that dataset in your hands. The study answers for the <b>average local income</b>. You can answer for <b>your own</b>: type what you earn, choose how much of it you would spend on housing, pick a mortgage term and a down payment, and the map, the rankings and the comparison table are recalculated for you. Or turn it around: say how many square metres you want and see where in Europe they are within reach.</p>
    <p>Everything is computed in your browser from one embedded table. Nothing is sent anywhere. The <b>Where the numbers come from</b> section below says exactly what was taken from where, and what was added.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── calculator ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="panel" id="p-calc" aria-labelledby="calc-h">
    <div class="phead">
      <div class="pactions"><button type="button" class="ibtn" data-share title="Copy a link to this setup" aria-label="Copy a link to this setup">{{svgShare}}</button></div>
      <h2 id="calc-h">Your numbers</h2>
      <p>The study assumes the average local income and a 30-year mortgage. Change any of it. With no income entered, every place is shown on its own average income, exactly as in the published maps.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="presets" id="presets" role="group" aria-label="Example setups"></div>
    <div class="calc">
      <div class="field f-income">
        <label for="inc">Net income of the household per month</label>
        <div class="inrow">
          <input id="inc" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" step="50" placeholder="leave empty for the local average">
          <select id="cur" aria-label="Currency"></select>
        </div>
        <p class="fhint" id="inchint">After tax, all earners together. Converted to euro at the ECB reference rate of 11 September 2026.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="share">Share of income for housing <output for="share" id="share-o">33 %</output></label>
        <input id="share" type="range" min="20" max="45" step="1" value="33">
        <p class="fhint">The study uses one third. Above 40 % is usually called an overburden.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="term">Mortgage term</label>
        <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Mortgage term in years" id="term">
          <button type="button" data-v="10">10 y</button><button type="button" data-v="15">15 y</button><button type="button" data-v="20">20 y</button><button type="button" data-v="25">25 y</button><button type="button" data-v="30" aria-pressed="true">30 y</button>
        </div>
        <p class="fhint">The study's maps use 30 years; its Annex B repeats them for 20.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="rate">Interest rate, % per year</label>
        <div class="inrow">
          <input id="rate" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" max="25" step="0.05" placeholder="national rate from the study">
          <button type="button" class="minibtn" id="rate-x" hidden>national</button>
        </div>
        <p class="fhint" id="ratehint">Empty means each country's own fixed rate from the study: 3.01 % in France, 4.00 % in Germany, 8.32 % in Poland.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="dep">Down payment <output for="dep" id="dep-o">0 %</output></label>
        <input id="dep" type="range" min="0" max="40" step="5" value="0">
        <p class="fhint">Of the price including taxes and fees. The study assumes none; the loan then covers the rest.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label>Household</label>
        <div class="inrow hh">
          <span class="stepper"><button type="button" data-hh="adults" data-d="-1" aria-label="Fewer adults">−</button><b id="adults-o">1</b><button type="button" data-hh="adults" data-d="1" aria-label="More adults">+</button><i>adults</i></span>
          <span class="stepper"><button type="button" data-hh="kids" data-d="-1" aria-label="Fewer children">−</button><b id="kids-o">0</b><button type="button" data-hh="kids" data-d="1" aria-label="More children">+</button><i>children under 14</i></span>
        </div>
        <p class="fhint" id="hhhint">Equivalence factor 1.0 (OECD-modified scale). Used only to compare your income with the local average per adult-equivalent.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field f-want">
        <label for="want">I want at least <output for="want" id="want-o">—</output></label>
        <input id="want" type="range" min="0" max="150" step="5" value="0">
        <p class="fhint">Zero switches the filter off. With a value, the map dims every region where that size is out of reach, and the rankings show only the places where it is not.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="setupline" id="setupline" aria-live="polite"></div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── map ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="panel" id="p-map" aria-labelledby="map-h">
    <div class="phead">
      <div class="pactions"><button type="button" class="ibtn" data-share title="Copy a link to this setup" aria-label="Copy a link to this setup">{{svgShare}}</button><button type="button" class="ibtn" data-png="map" title="Copy the map as a PNG" aria-label="Copy the map as a PNG">{{svgPng}}</button><button type="button" class="ibtn" data-png-dl="map" title="Download the map as a PNG" aria-label="Download the map as a PNG">{{svgDl}}</button><button type="button" class="ibtn" data-print="map" title="Print the map" aria-label="Print the map">{{svgPrint}}</button></div>
      <h2 id="map-h">The map</h2>
      <p>Countries are filled with their population-weighted average; each dot is a town, coloured on the same scale. Hover or tap either for its numbers, and zoom in for more towns. Search a town to jump straight to it. Red always means the harder place, whichever measure is showing.</p>
      <p>The last two measures answer the questions people actually ask. <b>Years of income</b> is how many years of gross income the home costs outright, and <b>rent share</b> is what renting it takes out of a month's income. Both are computed for the size you set under "I want", not for some invented typical flat, and both work wherever a price per square metre exists.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bar">
      <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="What the map shows" id="mapmode">
        <button type="button" data-v="buy" aria-pressed="true">m² to buy</button><button type="button" data-v="rent" aria-pressed="false">m² to rent</button><button type="button" data-v="diff" aria-pressed="false">Rent − buy</button><button type="button" data-v="years" aria-pressed="false">Years of income</button><button type="button" data-v="share" aria-pressed="false">Rent share</button>
      </div>
      <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Whose income" id="basis">
        <button type="button" data-v="local" aria-pressed="true">Local average income</button><button type="button" data-v="mine" aria-pressed="false" disabled title="Enter your income above">My income</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="gsearch">
      <label class="sr-only" for="q">Search a town, region or country</label>
      <input id="q" type="text" placeholder="Town, region or country — e.g. Porto, Bavaria, Poland" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" role="combobox" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="qsug" aria-autocomplete="list">
      <button type="button" class="gq-clear" id="qx" aria-label="Clear search" hidden>×</button>
      <ul class="gsug" id="qsug" role="listbox" aria-label="Matching places" hidden></ul>
    </div>
    <div class="mapwrap">
      <div class="mapbox" id="mapbox">
        <svg id="map" viewBox="0 0 {{geoW}} {{geoH}}" role="img" aria-label="Map of Europe: countries filled and towns marked as dots, coloured by affordable square metres">
          <g id="mapg">
            <g id="regions"></g>
            <g id="marks"></g>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <div class="legend" id="legend" aria-label="Map legend"></div>
        <div class="zoombar">
          <button type="button" class="zbtn" id="zin" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button>
          <button type="button" class="zbtn" id="zout" aria-label="Zoom out">−</button>
          <button type="button" class="zbtn" id="zreset" aria-label="Reset the view" title="Reset the view">⌂</button>
        </div>
        <div class="ghint"><span class="ghint-mouse">drag to pan · ctrl + wheel to zoom</span><span class="ghint-touch">drag sideways · pinch to zoom</span></div>
        <div class="tip" id="maptip" role="status"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cardcol" id="card">
        <p class="plabel">Selected place</p>
        <p class="cempty">Search a town above or click a region on the map. The card shows what your settings mean there, and what it would take.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="espon">Affordability data: © ESPON · Origin of data: ESPON EGTC. The interpretation of ESPON material does not necessarily reflect the opinion of the ESPON Monitoring Committee. The map on this page is drawn here from that data; it is not an ESPON map and does not use the ESPON map design. Country outlines: Natural Earth, public domain.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── compare ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="panel" id="p-cmp" aria-labelledby="cmp-h">
    <div class="phead">
      <div class="pactions"><button type="button" class="ibtn" data-share title="Copy a link to this setup" aria-label="Copy a link to this setup">{{svgShare}}</button><button type="button" class="ibtn" data-png="cmp" title="Copy the comparison as a PNG" aria-label="Copy the comparison as a PNG">{{svgPng}}</button><button type="button" class="ibtn" data-png-dl="cmp" title="Download the comparison as a PNG" aria-label="Download the comparison as a PNG">{{svgDl}}</button><button type="button" class="ibtn" data-csv="cmp" title="Download the comparison as CSV" aria-label="Download the comparison as CSV">{{svgCsv}}</button><button type="button" class="ibtn" data-print="cmp" title="Print the comparison" aria-label="Print the comparison">{{svgPrint}}</button></div>
      <h2 id="cmp-h">Side by side</h2>
      <p>Up to four places, towns or countries. Add them from the card above or from the rankings below. The first block follows your settings; the second holds the terms fixed so the places can be compared the way the study compares them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="chips" id="chips"></div>
    <div class="tablescroll"><table class="cmptable" id="cmptable"></table></div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── rankings ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="panel" id="p-rank" aria-labelledby="rank-h">
    <div class="phead">
      <div class="pactions"><button type="button" class="ibtn" data-share title="Copy a link to this setup" aria-label="Copy a link to this setup">{{svgShare}}</button><button type="button" class="ibtn" data-csv="rank" title="Download this table as CSV" aria-label="Download this table as CSV">{{svgCsv}}</button><button type="button" class="ibtn" data-print="rank" title="Print the table" aria-label="Print the table">{{svgPrint}}</button></div>
      <h2 id="rank-h">Rankings</h2>
      <p>Countries as population-weighted means of their municipalities, cities as single municipalities of 100,000 people or more. Every number moves with your settings; the size filter above narrows the list.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bar">
      <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="What to rank" id="rankwhat">
        <button type="button" data-v="countries" aria-pressed="true">Countries</button><button type="button" data-v="cities" aria-pressed="false">Cities</button>
      </div>
      <div class="regs" role="group" aria-label="Parts of Europe" id="regs"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tablescroll"><table class="ranktable" id="ranktable"><thead><tr id="rankhead"></tr></thead><tbody id="rankbody"></tbody></table></div>
    <p class="note" id="ranknote"></p>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── figure 3 ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="panel" id="p-hist" aria-labelledby="hist-h">
    <div class="phead">
