      <p>The study's figure 3, rebuilt from the same table: each bar is a class of affordability, its height the share of the population of the 31 countries living there, its colours the split into cities, towns and suburbs, and rural areas. Fixed to the study's own terms: a third of the local average income, 30 years, national rate. Your settings do not move this chart.</p>
